        "Content": "A recently sympathetically restored and tastefully renovated traditional style 2 storey detached stone cottage on 4.4 acres (ideal for a pony or a hobby farmer) with sea view and a woodland garden directly opposite. The cottage is in pristine condition throughout and the level of materials and craftmanship is second to none. The property also has a detached 2 storey stone outbuilding (ideal for conversion to either ancillary living space, a home office, an artist's studio or stables - the list goes on and on). There is also and a recently constructed workshop/storage facility and a stone utility building\r\n\r\n\r\nLOCATION: \r\nThe property is located within walking distance of 2 bars (one with a restaurant and the other with an award winning beer garden); the Ahakista Pier; the Air India Memorial Garden; 2 beaches and an art gallery with café and gardens. The market town of Bantry is 20 minutes by car and Cork City and airport are just over one and a half hours by car. The area is served by local transport - 5 round trip buses pass through Ahakista daily enroute from Kilcrohane via Bantry to Castletownbere\r\n\r\nTHE ACCOMMODATION: \r\nThe 138 sq/m (1,485 sq.ft) property is in excellent condition, having been totally renovated over the past few years and is now awaiting its new occupant! All rooms have column style radiators. All windows are double glazed with black wood grain uPVC \r\n\r\nDownstairs: 87.29 s/m (940 sq. ft)\r\nall floors are Brazilian slate \r\n\r\nopen plan kitchen (4.690m x 4.620m)/dining area (5m x 3.820m) - sea view, vaulted ceiling in kitchen, custom made painted kitchen units and centre island, silestone counter top, Belfast sink, integrated dishwasher, electric range, integrated fridge/freezer, recessed lighting in dining area, TV point, door to outside \r\n\r\nliving room - 4.260m x 4.5m - sea view, wood burning stove, recessed lighting, shelving in alcoves, TV point \r\n\r\nshower room - 3.025m x 1.410m - large shower tray (1400 mm x 900 mm), wash basin, WC, west facing window \r\n\r\nutility room - 2.625m x 2.970m - door to outside, north and east facing windows and velux, double Belfast sink, fitted cabinets, plumbed for washing machine \r\n\r\nutility cupboard/hot press - 2.625m x 0.9m - with pressurised cylinder and an 'Aquabox' for additional water storage \r\n\r\nUpstairs: 50.79 s/m (535 sq. ft.) \r\nall floors are timber with the exception of the bathroom \r\n\r\ndouble bedroom no. 1 - 4.310m x 4.050m - west facing window with sea view, east facing window with countryside and mountain view, velux window \r\n\r\nbathroom - 2820m x 3060m with tub, shower, hand basin and WC, velux window \r\n\r\ndouble bedroom no. 2 - 2.680m x 4.9m - west facing window with sea view and velux window \r\n\r\nDETACHED 2 STOREY STONE OUTBUILDING WITH QUARRY SLATED ROOF: \r\nInternal measurement 8.9m x 3.44m Floor to ceiling height downstairs - 1.94m and upstairs 2.875m from floor joists to apex This building has a treated water, foul drainage and electricity connection. Subject to receipt of the necessary planning permission, it could be converted to ancillary living accommodation or a very comfortable stable for a pony or two! \r\n\r\nDETACHED WORKSHOP WITH ATTACHED WOOD SHED: \r\nexternal measurement of workshop - 4.9m x 5.22m - double doors, electricity - lights and sockets external measurement of wood shed - 3.65m x 5.05m \r\n\r\nPlease note that all measurements are approximate \r\n\r\nSERVICES & UPGRADES: \r\noil fired central heating in all rooms - new boiler and new radiators \r\nwood burner in living room \r\nnewly bored well with new pump and filtration system pressurised water cylinder with extra water capacity via an 'Aquabox' \r\nnew plumbing \r\nnewly commissioned and certified waste water system \r\nnew wiring \r\nnew kitchen and bathrooms \r\nfully insulated"
      },
